## Exit-code contract pinned by the CLI guard (process level, isolated evidence dir)
  0 = unchanged (no write)        1 = invalid mapping/convention violation (no write, names walkerPath)
  2 = changed/stale mapping (no write, prints diff)   3 = missing mapping (no write, names --refresh)
  --refresh = explicit bootstrap/write; the next run is then unchanged (0, no write).
  Note: the CLI guard spawns asynchronously; spawnSync blocked the vitest worker event loop and produced a
  worker RPC timeout (exit 1) even with all assertions passing, which is why this suite previously misreported.

